  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. organic chemical exports rose 14.1% to $59.18B in 2025, led by hormones and steroids (2937, $19.09B, up 91.6%); Italy alone bought $16.04B.",
    "The EU is 49% of the chapter and has charged U.S. chemicals nothing since July 1, 2026 (mannitol and sorbitol excepted); Mexico, Canada and South Korea also charge nothing on qualifying goods.",
    "China is the only large buyer that raised tariffs — a 10% extra duty on all U.S. goods — and U.S. exports there fell 13.3% to $3.45B; India's February 2026 framework promises cuts but none is in force.",
    "Before shipping, check TSCA section 12(b) export notices, DEA rules for listed chemicals and controlled substances, and the Chemical Weapons Convention controls; the buyer's chemical-registration regime decides whether the cargo can be sold."
  ],
